   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    43.46,
    48.75,
    568.55,
    69.4
   ],
   "text": "Evidence-Anchored Reading Order for Two-Column Scientific Documents",
   "role": "heading",
   "column": -1,
   "reading_order": 1,
   "font_size": 15.0,
   "n_chars": 67,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b3",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    54.51,
    79.25,
    557.49,
    105.99
   ],
   "text": "We present a deterministic parser that recovers the true reading order of two-column scientific pages and anchors\nevery block to a page and bounding box.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": -1,
   "reading_order": 2,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 153,
   "flags": [
    "merged:p1_b4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b5",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    50.4,
    130.45,
    287.74,
    180.19
   ],
   "text": "L1 Introduction. Scientific documents frequently use a\ntwo-column layout. A naive top-to-bottom text\nextraction interleaves the columns and produces\nbroken sentences.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 0,
   "reading_order": 3,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 166,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b7",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    50.4,
    213.25,
    294.4,
    262.99
   ],
   "text": "L2 Method. We cluster text blocks by horizontal\nposition, treat full-width blocks as band separators, and\norder each column from top to bottom before moving\nright.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 0,
   "reading_order": 4,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 163,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b9",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    50.4,
    296.05,
    290.52,
    333.79
   ],
   "text": "L3 Anchoring. Every emitted block keeps its page\nnumber and bounding box so that any downstream\nanswer can be traced back to the exact source region.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 0,
   "reading_order": 5,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 149,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b6",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    316.8,
    130.45,
    551.35,
    180.19
   ],
   "text": "R1 Evaluation. On a controlled document with known\nground truth we measure character recall and\nreading-order concordance against the intended\nsequence.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 1,
   "reading_order": 6,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 152,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b8",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    316.8,
    213.25,
    560.22,
    250.99
   ],
   "text": "R2 Results. The parser recovers essentially all body\ncharacters and preserves the column-major reading\norder, while a naive y-sort interleaves the two columns.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 1,
   "reading_order": 7,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 159,
   "flags": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p1_b10",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": [
    316.8,
    296.05,
    558.01,
    333.79
   ],
   "text": "R3 Limitations. Image-only scanned pages have no\ntext layer and require OCR, which is outside the scope\nof this text-layer parser and is reported as unreadable.",
   "role": "body",
   "column": 1,
   "reading_order": 8,
   "font_size": 10.0,
   "n_chars": 160,
   "flags": []
  },
